From: AltarsCN <337293323+Altars3668@users.noreply.github.com>
Date: Sun, 27 Sep 2026 21:44:33 -0400
Subject: [PATCH] d2d1: Antialias what is drawn with
 D2D1_ANTIALIAS_MODE_PER_PRIMITIVE.

SetAntialiasMode() was recorded and nothing more: every fill and stroke,
and every clip, was aliased, which in Office leaves every shape, chart line
and gradient-filled word with stepped edges.  Windows covers a pixel by as
much of it as the primitive covers (tools/d2daaprobe in wine-altars, build
29671): 0.75 of it for an edge at x + 0.25, 178/255 for a clip edge at
x + 0.3, and a line a pixel wide at an angle smeared over its row.

Each primitive is now drawn first into a mask of what it covers over the
pixels its bounds, or widened bounds, and the clip reach: R8, with 8
samples, or as many as the device has; the mask, kept by the context and
grown as needed, is cleared over them with ClearView().  The edges of
triangles are covered by the samples; those the pixel shader decides --
curves, curved strokes and round joins -- cover as much of the pixel as is
within them, the distance to the edge in pixels being the implicit
function over its gradient, rather than clipping at the pixel's centre.
The mask keeps the most any part covers, so the parts of one primitive do
not add up where they overlap.  Then a rectangle over those pixels is drawn
with the brush, times the mean of the mask's samples.  A rectangle along
the edges of pixels is drawn as before.

An axis-aligned clip pushed antialiased keeps as much of each pixel as it
covers, worked out in the pixel shader, edge by edge from whichever clip
the edge of the intersection comes from.  Clearing keeps to the pixels
whose centres the clip keeps, as before.

A rectangle and a clip antialiased now match Windows exactly; an edge of a
triangle is within an eighth of a pixel, curves within a few percent.  The
new test passes on Windows, in a desktop session on the GPU, and with the
GL and Vulkan renderers.

Per-sample shading was tried first and dropped: the renderers do not agree
with each other or with Windows on where a per-sample shader's inputs and
SV_Position are (tools/d3d11sampleprobe in wine-altars).

Co-Authored-By: Claude Opus 5.5 <noreply@anthropic.com>
(cherry picked from commit 69802d1f7ce8c79b1567b82c2f8a0e2421d3f859)

